  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "frame_get_lazychunk",
    "file": "c-blosc2/blosc/frame.c",
    "description": "In the in-memory contiguous-frame branch, `frame_get_lazychunk` checks only that `header_len + offset + BLOSC_MIN_HEADER_LENGTH` is within `frame->len`, then reads and returns the chunk header's attacker-controlled `cbytes` without verifying that `header_len + offset + cbytes` is within the actual frame buffer. `frame_decompress_chunk` consequently passes this forged size to `blosc2_decompress_ctx`. Its source-size checks trust that value, so a malicious block start can place `src` beyond the allocation and `blosc_d` performs the out-of-bounds 4-byte `sw32_` read at blosc2.c:1349.",
    "conditions": "A fuzzer-supplied buffer must parse as an in-memory contiguous frame with at least one decompressed chunk. The chunk offset must be accepted and leave enough real bytes for a minimum Blosc header, while that header declares a `cbytes` larger than the bytes remaining in `frame->cframe`. A non-memcpy compressed chunk with attacker-controlled block-start metadata must then select an offset that is below the forged `cbytes`/`srcsize` but outside the actual input allocation. During `blosc2_schunk_decompress_chunk` -> `frame_decompress_chunk` -> `blosc2_decompress_ctx`, the false size defeats bounds checks and `blosc_d` reads a stream compressed-size word out of bounds."
  },
